<?php
// Long-form report knowledge base (en). Generated; edit the source tables, not by hand.
return [
'planet' => ['Sun' => ['sig' => 'The Sun is the soul of the horoscope and the king among the planets. It represents your father, authority, government, self-confidence, vitality, bones, eyes and the heart. It shows how you shine in the world, your sense of dignity and the kind of respect you earn. A well-placed Sun gives courage, leadership and a clear sense of purpose in life.', 'strong' => 'When the Sun is strong you are confident, principled and naturally take charge. Support from father, seniors and government comes more easily, and your reputation grows steadily with age. Health is usually robust and you recover quickly from illness.', 'weak' => 'When the Sun is weak or afflicted, confidence can swing between pride and self-doubt. Friction with father, bosses or officials, delays in recognition and low energy are common signs. Heart, eyes and bones need regular care, and ego clashes are best avoided.', 'dasha' => 'The Sun\'s mahadasha lasts six years and brings status, authority and self-expression to the front. Promotions, government work, dealings with powerful people and matters of the father come up. With a strong Sun this period brings honour and position; with a weak Sun it brings pressure from authority and a need to look after health.', 'remedy' => 'Offer water to the rising Sun every morning, respect your father and elders, and never lie or misuse authority. Donating wheat, jaggery or copper on Sundays and reciting the Aditya Hridaya Stotra strengthen the Sun.', 'deity' => 'Surya Dev', 'day' => 'Sunday', 'color' => 'Red, saffron', 'gem' => 'Ruby (Manik)', 'metal' => 'Copper, gold', 'grain' => 'Wheat', 'number' => '1', 'mantra' => 'ॐ सूर्याय नमः'], 'Moon' => ['sig' => 'The Moon is the mind and the mother. It rules emotions, memory, sleep, the fluids of the body, comfort, public life and your bond with your mother. In Vedic astrology the Moon sign is as important as the ascendant, because it shows how you feel and react from moment to moment. A calm, strong Moon is the basis of a happy life.', 'strong' => 'A strong Moon gives emotional balance, a caring nature, a good memory and popularity with people. You adapt easily, sleep well and receive help from your mother and from women in general. Public-facing work often goes well.', 'weak' => 'A weak or afflicted Moon shows as mood swings, worry, disturbed sleep and over-sensitivity. Cold, cough, water-related ailments and hormonal imbalance may trouble you, and peace of mind needs conscious effort and a steady routine.', 'dasha' => 'The Moon\'s mahadasha lasts ten years and brings home, mother, emotions, travel and public dealings into focus. A strong Moon makes this period comfortable, prosperous and emotionally fulfilling. A weak Moon asks you to protect your peace of mind and your health.', 'remedy' => 'Respect your mother and take her blessings, keep a piece of silver with you, and offer water or milk to Lord Shiva on Mondays. Donating rice, milk or white clothes and chanting the Moon mantra calm the mind.', 'deity' => 'Lord Shiva, Mother Parvati', 'day' => 'Monday', 'color' => 'White', 'gem' => 'Pearl (Moti)', 'metal' => 'Silver', 'grain' => 'Rice', 'number' => '2', 'mantra' => 'ॐ चन्द्राय नमः'], 'Mars' => ['sig' => 'Mars is the commander among the planets: energy, courage, action and drive. It rules brothers, land and property, police and army, sports, surgery, blood and muscles. Mars shows how you fight for what you want and how you handle anger and competition. Used well, it is the engine of every achievement.', 'strong' => 'A strong Mars gives courage, stamina, quick decisions and success in property, engineering, sports or uniformed services. You protect others, finish what you start and are not afraid of hard work or competition.', 'weak' => 'A weak or afflicted Mars can bring anger, accidents, cuts and burns, disputes over land and friction with siblings. Blood pressure and inflammation need watching, and hasty actions or harsh words should be avoided.', 'dasha' => 'The Mars mahadasha lasts seven years and is a time of action: property deals, competitive exams, new ventures and physical effort. Well placed, it brings land, courage and victory over rivals. Badly placed, it brings disputes, injuries and haste that must be controlled.', 'remedy' => 'Recite the Hanuman Chalisa, keep good relations with your brothers, and donate red lentils (masoor) or jaggery on Tuesdays. Avoid anger and harsh speech; regular physical exercise channels the energy of Mars positively.', 'deity' => 'Lord Hanuman, Kartikeya', 'day' => 'Tuesday', 'color' => 'Red', 'gem' => 'Red Coral (Moonga)', 'metal' => 'Copper', 'grain' => 'Red lentils', 'number' => '9', 'mantra' => 'ॐ भौमाय नमः'], 'Mercury' => ['sig' => 'Mercury is the prince among the planets: intelligence, speech, writing, trade, calculation and learning. It rules friends, sisters, maternal relatives, the skin and the nervous system. Mercury shows how you think, how you communicate and how you make deals. A clear Mercury makes every other skill easier to use.', 'strong' => 'A strong Mercury gives sharp intelligence, good humour, skill with numbers and words, and success in business, writing, media, accounts or teaching. You learn quickly, adapt to people and can explain things well.', 'weak' => 'A weak Mercury can cause confusion, nervousness, speech or skin problems, and losses through wrong calculations or untrustworthy friends. Signatures, contracts and gossip need extra care, and decisions should be double-checked.', 'dasha' => 'Mercury\'s mahadasha lasts seventeen years and favours education, trade, communication and networking. With good placement it brings business growth, new skills and clever gains. With weak placement it brings scattered effort, nervous strain and the need for careful paperwork.', 'remedy' => 'Worship Lord Ganesha, feed green grass to cows, and donate green moong on Wednesdays. Keep your word, avoid gossip, and respect your sisters and aunts; these simple acts keep Mercury pleased.', 'deity' => 'Lord Vishnu, Lord Ganesha', 'day' => 'Wednesday', 'color' => 'Green', 'gem' => 'Emerald (Panna)', 'metal' => 'Bronze', 'grain' => 'Green moong', 'number' => '5', 'mantra' => 'ॐ बुधाय नमः'], 'Jupiter' => ['sig' => 'Jupiter is the guru: wisdom, knowledge, faith, children, wealth and good fortune. It rules teachers, priests, higher education, law, the liver and fat in the body. Jupiter shows where life protects you and where growth comes naturally. Its blessing is the most valued protection in any horoscope.', 'strong' => 'A strong Jupiter gives wisdom, respect, a moral outlook, good children and steady wealth. Teachers and elders guide you, and difficulties are overcome with divine help. You are often trusted as an adviser.', 'weak' => 'A weak Jupiter can bring poor judgement, delays in children or marriage, lack of guidance, and problems with the liver, weight or sugar. Over-optimism and lack of discipline with money need care.', 'dasha' => 'Jupiter\'s mahadasha lasts sixteen years and is often a period of growth: marriage, children, higher studies, spiritual interest and increase in wealth. Its placement decides how smoothly these blessings arrive and how much effort they need.', 'remedy' => 'Respect teachers and elders, apply a saffron or turmeric tilak, and donate yellow items such as chana dal or turmeric on Thursdays. Reading scriptures and serving learned people strengthen Jupiter.', 'deity' => 'Brihaspati, Lord Vishnu', 'day' => 'Thursday', 'color' => 'Yellow', 'gem' => 'Yellow Sapphire (Pukhraj)', 'metal' => 'Gold', 'grain' => 'Chana dal', 'number' => '3', 'mantra' => 'ॐ गुरवे नमः'], 'Venus' => ['sig' => 'Venus is the planet of love, beauty, comfort and luxury. It rules marriage and the spouse, art, music, fashion, vehicles, perfumes and the reproductive system. Venus shows what you enjoy, how you relate in love and how much comfort life gives you. It is also the teacher of the demons, wise in worldly matters.', 'strong' => 'A strong Venus gives charm, artistic talent, a happy married life, comforts, vehicles and refined taste. Earnings through art, beauty, hospitality or luxury goods are favoured, and people are drawn to you.', 'weak' => 'A weak Venus can bring delays or unhappiness in marriage, over-indulgence, and problems with the kidneys, sugar or reproductive system. Money may go on luxuries, and relationships need honesty and balance.', 'dasha' => 'Venus\' mahadasha is the longest, twenty years, and brings marriage, comforts, property, vehicles and creative success. Good placement makes it a period of prosperity and pleasure; weak placement asks for moderation in relationships and spending.', 'remedy' => 'Respect your spouse and all women, keep yourself and your home clean and fragrant, and donate white items such as rice, curd or white clothes on Fridays. Worship of Goddess Lakshmi strengthens Venus.', 'deity' => 'Goddess Lakshmi', 'day' => 'Friday', 'color' => 'White, pink', 'gem' => 'Diamond (Heera) or Opal', 'metal' => 'Silver', 'grain' => 'Rice', 'number' => '6', 'mantra' => 'ॐ शुक्राय नमः'], 'Saturn' => ['sig' => 'Saturn is the judge: discipline, hard work, patience, time and karma. It rules servants and workers, labour, oil and iron, old age, longevity, and the legs, bones and nerves. Saturn gives results slowly but permanently, exactly according to your actions. It rewards honesty and punishes shortcuts.', 'strong' => 'A strong Saturn gives patience, responsibility, endurance and success that lasts. You rise through steady work, gain from land, industry or service, and earn respect as a fair and reliable person.', 'weak' => 'A weak Saturn brings delays, hard work with little recognition, loneliness, and pain in joints, legs or teeth. Sade Sati and Dhaiya periods feel heavier, and shortcuts or dishonesty bring quick setbacks.', 'dasha' => 'Saturn\'s mahadasha lasts nineteen years and rewards discipline and honest effort. Well placed, it builds a lasting career, property and status. Badly placed, it tests patience with delays, health issues and heavy responsibilities.', 'remedy' => 'Serve labourers and the elderly, donate mustard oil, black sesame or black urad on Saturdays, and light a mustard-oil lamp under a peepal tree. Avoid alcohol, lying and cheating; honesty is the strongest remedy for Saturn.', 'deity' => 'Shani Dev, Lord Hanuman', 'day' => 'Saturday', 'color' => 'Black, dark blue', 'gem' => 'Blue Sapphire (Neelam)', 'metal' => 'Iron', 'grain' => 'Black sesame, urad', 'number' => '8', 'mantra' => 'ॐ शनैश्चराय नमः'], 'Rahu' => ['sig' => 'Rahu is the north node of the Moon, a shadow planet of desire, ambition, illusion and the unconventional. It rules foreign lands, technology, politics, sudden events, research and anything new or unusual. Rahu magnifies the house it occupies and creates a strong hunger for its matters. Handled with clarity, it can lift you very high.', 'strong' => 'A well-placed Rahu gives bold ambition, success in politics, technology, foreign trade or media, and sudden gains. You think out of the box and seize new opportunities quickly.', 'weak' => 'An afflicted Rahu brings confusion, fear, addictions, deception by others and sudden setbacks. Mental unrest, skin problems and trouble from hidden enemies are possible, so clarity and honest dealings are essential.', 'dasha' => 'Rahu\'s mahadasha lasts eighteen years and brings sudden changes: foreign travel, new fields, a rapid rise or unexpected turns. Its results depend strongly on the house and sign it occupies and on the planet that rules that sign.', 'remedy' => 'Worship Goddess Durga or Saraswati, keep your head covered at religious places, and donate coconut, barley or dark cloth. Avoid alcohol and shortcuts; staying truthful keeps Rahu under control.', 'deity' => 'Goddess Durga', 'day' => 'Saturday', 'color' => 'Grey, smoky blue', 'gem' => 'Hessonite (Gomed)', 'metal' => 'Lead', 'grain' => 'Barley', 'number' => '4', 'mantra' => 'ॐ राहवे नमः'], 'Ketu' => ['sig' => 'Ketu is the south node of the Moon: detachment, spirituality, past-life skills and sudden insight. It rules intuition, research, occult knowledge, sons and maternal grandparents, and small animals such as dogs. Ketu brings sudden events and a feeling that something is missing in the house it occupies, pushing you to look deeper.', 'strong' => 'A well-placed Ketu gives sharp intuition, spiritual depth, research ability and freedom from greed. Past-life talents appear easily, and you can let go of what no longer serves you.', 'weak' => 'An afflicted Ketu can bring confusion, loss of interest, isolation, sudden injuries and health issues that are hard to diagnose. Decisions made in haste or out of indifference can cause loss.', 'dasha' => 'Ketu\'s mahadasha lasts seven years and often turns the mind inward: spirituality, research, pilgrimages and letting go of attachments. It can bring sudden changes and is best used for inner growth and learning.', 'remedy' => 'Worship Lord Ganesha, feed dogs, and donate a black-and-white blanket or sesame at a temple. Applying a saffron tilak and meditating regularly calm Ketu.', 'deity' => 'Lord Ganesha', 'day' => 'Tuesday', 'color' => 'Multicolour, grey', 'gem' => 'Cat\'s eye (Lahsuniya)', 'metal' => 'Mixed metals', 'grain' => 'Sesame', 'number' => '7', 'mantra' => 'ॐ केतवे नमः']],
'sign' => ['Aries' => ['el' => 'Fire', 'mod' => 'Movable', 'body' => 'head', 'nature' => 'Aries is the first sign of the zodiac: fiery, bold and pioneering, symbolised by the ram. It loves new beginnings, speed and challenge.', 'lagna' => 'With Aries rising you have an active, energetic body and a direct, courageous personality. You like to lead, act quickly and speak frankly, and you dislike waiting. Your face often shows determination, and the head is a sensitive area for health. Learning patience and finishing what you start turns your drive into real success.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in Aries your emotions are quick, warm and honest. You react instantly, get angry fast but also forgive fast, and feel happiest when you are doing something. You need independence and excitement, and routine or restriction makes you restless.'], 'Taurus' => ['el' => 'Earth', 'mod' => 'Fixed', 'body' => 'face and throat', 'nature' => 'Taurus is steady, practical and pleasure-loving, symbolised by the bull. It values security, comfort, beauty and loyalty.', 'lagna' => 'With Taurus rising you have a calm, steady nature and a pleasant, well-built appearance. You are patient, practical and reliable, and you enjoy good food, music and comfort. You dislike sudden change and can be stubborn once you decide. The throat and neck need care, and steady routines keep you healthy.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in Taurus, its sign of exaltation, your emotions are stable, loyal and grounded. You find peace in home, nature, good food and financial security. Once attached you stay attached, and you give practical, dependable care to those you love.'], 'Gemini' => ['el' => 'Air', 'mod' => 'Dual', 'body' => 'arms, shoulders and lungs', 'nature' => 'Gemini is curious, communicative and versatile, symbolised by the twins. It loves information, conversation, travel and variety.', 'lagna' => 'With Gemini rising you are quick-witted, talkative and youthful in appearance and manner. You learn fast, adapt to people easily and can handle many things at once. Restlessness and scattered effort are your challenges. Nerves, lungs and hands need care, and focus brings out your many talents.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in Gemini your mind is lively, curious and always seeking new ideas. You process feelings by talking and thinking about them, and you need mental stimulation to feel content. Moods change quickly, and friends and conversation play a big part in your happiness.'], 'Cancer' => ['el' => 'Water', 'mod' => 'Movable', 'body' => 'chest and stomach', 'nature' => 'Cancer is caring, sensitive and protective, symbolised by the crab. It values home, family, memory and emotional security.', 'lagna' => 'With Cancer rising you have a soft, caring nature and a gentle face. Family, home and emotional security are central to your life, and you protect those you love fiercely. You are intuitive and imaginative but can be moody or over-sensitive. The chest and stomach need care, and a peaceful home keeps you strong.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in its own sign Cancer, your emotions are deep, nurturing and very responsive. You feel the moods of others and care for them naturally. Home and mother mean a great deal to you, and you need emotional security to perform your best.'], 'Leo' => ['el' => 'Fire', 'mod' => 'Fixed', 'body' => 'heart and spine', 'nature' => 'Leo is royal, generous and confident, symbolised by the lion. It loves recognition, creativity, leadership and loyalty.', 'lagna' => 'With Leo rising you have a dignified bearing, a strong presence and a generous heart. You like to lead, to be respected and to do things in a grand way. Pride and a need for appreciation can cause friction, but your loyalty and warmth win people over. The heart and spine need care, and a purpose larger than yourself brings out your best.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in Leo your emotions are warm, proud and expressive. You need to feel appreciated and you give generously to those who value you. Hurt pride affects you deeply, and creative expression and admiration from loved ones keep you happy.'], 'Virgo' => ['el' => 'Earth', 'mod' => 'Dual', 'body' => 'intestines and digestion', 'nature' => 'Virgo is analytical, practical and service-minded, symbolised by the maiden. It values precision, health, order and useful work.', 'lagna' => 'With Virgo rising you are neat, careful and intelligent, with a youthful look and a practical mind. You notice details, solve problems and like to be useful. Worry and over-criticism of yourself or others are your challenges. Digestion and nerves need care, and a healthy daily routine keeps you well.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in Virgo your feelings are expressed through care, service and practical help. You analyse emotions rather than show them openly, and you feel secure when life is organised. Worry can build up, so routine, good health habits and useful work calm your mind.'], 'Libra' => ['el' => 'Air', 'mod' => 'Movable', 'body' => 'kidneys and lower back', 'nature' => 'Libra is balanced, diplomatic and artistic, symbolised by the scales. It values harmony, partnership, justice and beauty.', 'lagna' => 'With Libra rising you are graceful, polite and fair-minded, with a pleasant appearance and good taste. Partnerships matter greatly and you work best with others. Indecision and a wish to please everyone can slow you down. The kidneys and lower back need care, and balance between work and rest keeps you healthy.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in Libra your emotional peace depends on harmony and good relationships. You dislike conflict and try to keep everyone happy, sometimes at your own cost. Beauty, art and a loving partner nourish your mind.'], 'Scorpio' => ['el' => 'Water', 'mod' => 'Fixed', 'body' => 'reproductive and excretory organs', 'nature' => 'Scorpio is intense, secretive and transformative, symbolised by the scorpion. It values depth, loyalty, research and hidden power.', 'lagna' => 'With Scorpio rising you have a strong, magnetic personality and penetrating eyes. You are determined, private and deeply loyal, and you rarely forget either help or harm. Jealousy and suspicion are your challenges. The reproductive and excretory systems need care, and channelling your intensity into research or healing brings great success.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in Scorpio, its sign of debilitation, emotions run very deep and are often kept hidden. You feel strongly, trust slowly and can be affected by worry or suspicion. Spiritual practice, trusted relationships and meaningful work bring you emotional strength.'], 'Sagittarius' => ['el' => 'Fire', 'mod' => 'Dual', 'body' => 'hips, thighs and liver', 'nature' => 'Sagittarius is optimistic, philosophical and freedom-loving, symbolised by the archer. It values truth, faith, learning and travel.', 'lagna' => 'With Sagittarius rising you are honest, cheerful and idealistic, often with an open, friendly face. You love learning, travel, religion and philosophy, and you speak your mind. Over-confidence and bluntness can create problems. The hips, thighs and liver need care, and a meaningful goal keeps you energised.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in Sagittarius your mind is optimistic, generous and in search of meaning. You feel happiest with freedom, travel, study and faith. You bounce back quickly from setbacks, though restlessness can make commitment difficult.'], 'Capricorn' => ['el' => 'Earth', 'mod' => 'Movable', 'body' => 'knees, bones and joints', 'nature' => 'Capricorn is ambitious, disciplined and practical, symbolised by the sea-goat. It values responsibility, status, patience and long-term success.', 'lagna' => 'With Capricorn rising you are serious, hard-working and ambitious, often looking mature for your age. You build your life step by step, and success usually grows after the age of thirty. Pessimism and over-work are your challenges. The knees, bones and joints need care, and patience is your greatest strength.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in Capricorn your emotions are controlled, practical and responsible. You show love through duty and support rather than words. You may feel lonely at times, and achievement and security bring you emotional peace.'], 'Aquarius' => ['el' => 'Air', 'mod' => 'Fixed', 'body' => 'calves, ankles and circulation', 'nature' => 'Aquarius is humanitarian, original and independent, symbolised by the water-bearer. It values friendship, ideas, society and progress.', 'lagna' => 'With Aquarius rising you are friendly, thoughtful and original, with a keen interest in society and new ideas. You value freedom and like to help people in large groups. Detachment and stubbornness can create distance. The calves, ankles and circulation need care, and working for a cause gives you deep satisfaction.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in Aquarius your feelings are expressed through friendship, ideas and service to others. You need space and independence, and you can seem detached though you care deeply. Group activities and meaningful causes keep your mind happy.'], 'Pisces' => ['el' => 'Water', 'mod' => 'Dual', 'body' => 'feet and immunity', 'nature' => 'Pisces is compassionate, imaginative and spiritual, symbolised by two fish. It values faith, kindness, art and inner peace.', 'lagna' => 'With Pisces rising you are gentle, kind and imaginative, with soft, dreamy eyes. You are sensitive to the pain of others and often drawn to spirituality, art or healing. Escapism and weak boundaries are your challenges. The feet and immunity need care, and a spiritual routine keeps you grounded.', 'moon' => 'With the Moon in Pisces your emotions are tender, intuitive and compassionate. You absorb the moods around you, so peaceful company and spiritual practice are important. Imagination is strong and you give selflessly to those you love.']],
'house' => [1 => ['name' => 'Tanu Bhava', 'topics' => 'self, body, personality, health and appearance', 'about' => 'The first house is the foundation of the horoscope. It shows your body and health, your temperament, the way others see you and the general direction of your life. A strong first house and lord give confidence, vitality and the ability to overcome obstacles.'], 2 => ['name' => 'Dhana Bhava', 'topics' => 'wealth, family, speech, food, savings and early education', 'about' => 'The second house shows accumulated wealth, family values, speech and food habits. It indicates how you save, how you speak and the support you receive from family. It is also the house of early education and of the face.'], 3 => ['name' => 'Sahaja Bhava', 'topics' => 'courage, siblings, communication, short travel, skills and effort', 'about' => 'The third house shows your own efforts, courage and initiative. It rules younger siblings, communication, writing, media, short journeys and the hands. Planets here give drive and the ability to achieve through personal effort.'], 4 => ['name' => 'Sukha Bhava', 'topics' => 'mother, home, property, vehicles, happiness and basic education', 'about' => 'The fourth house is the house of happiness: mother, home, land, vehicles and inner peace. It also shows basic education and emotional security. A strong fourth house gives comfort, property and a supportive family base.'], 5 => ['name' => 'Putra Bhava', 'topics' => 'children, intelligence, creativity, romance, past merit and speculation', 'about' => 'The fifth house shows children, intelligence, creativity and love affairs. It is the house of purva punya, the merit carried from past lives, and of mantra, learning and speculation. It reveals how easily good fortune flows to you.'], 6 => ['name' => 'Ripu Bhava', 'topics' => 'health issues, enemies, debts, disputes, service and competition', 'about' => 'The sixth house shows illness, enemies, debts and competition, and your power to overcome them. It also rules daily work, service, employees and pets. Malefic planets here are good fighters and help you win over obstacles.'], 7 => ['name' => 'Kalatra Bhava', 'topics' => 'marriage, spouse, partnerships, business and public dealings', 'about' => 'The seventh house shows marriage and the life partner, business partnerships and all one-to-one relationships. It also indicates public dealings, travel and trade. Its condition reveals the nature of your spouse and your married life.'], 8 => ['name' => 'Ayu Bhava', 'topics' => 'longevity, sudden events, secrets, inheritance, research and the occult', 'about' => 'The eighth house rules longevity, sudden changes, hidden matters and transformation. It shows inheritance, insurance, the spouse\'s money, research and occult knowledge. Its planets can bring deep insight as well as unexpected events.'], 9 => ['name' => 'Dharma Bhava', 'topics' => 'luck, father, guru, religion, higher learning and long journeys', 'about' => 'The ninth house is the house of fortune and dharma: father, teachers, faith, higher education and long journeys. A strong ninth house brings luck, blessings and guidance, and helps your efforts bear fruit.'], 10 => ['name' => 'Karma Bhava', 'topics' => 'career, profession, status, authority, reputation and actions', 'about' => 'The tenth house is the house of karma and career. It shows your profession, status, authority, reputation and public achievements. Planets here and the tenth lord reveal the kind of work that suits you and how far you rise.'], 11 => ['name' => 'Labha Bhava', 'topics' => 'gains, income, elder siblings, friends, networks and wishes', 'about' => 'The eleventh house is the house of gains: income, profits, fulfilment of desires, friends and elder siblings. Almost every planet does well here, bringing money and support through networks and connections.'], 12 => ['name' => 'Vyaya Bhava', 'topics' => 'expenses, losses, foreign lands, sleep, spirituality and liberation', 'about' => 'The twelfth house shows expenses, losses, foreign lands, hospitals and isolation, and also sleep, pleasures of the bed, charity and liberation. It reveals where your energy and money flow out, and the path of your spiritual journey.']],
'nak' => ['Ashwini' => ['Ashwini Kumaras', 'a horse\'s head', 'Quick, energetic and healing, Ashwini natives love speed and new beginnings. They are helpful and youthful, and are often gifted in medicine or in solving problems quickly.'], 'Bharani' => ['Yama', 'the yoni', 'Bharani gives a strong will, creativity and the capacity to carry heavy responsibility. Natives are passionate and truthful, and can handle the extremes of life with courage.'], 'Krittika' => ['Agni', 'a razor or flame', 'Krittika is sharp, purifying and determined. Natives are courageous, direct and protective, with high standards for themselves and for others.'], 'Rohini' => ['Brahma', 'an ox-cart', 'Rohini is creative, attractive and fertile, the Moon\'s favourite star. Natives love beauty, comfort and art, and have a gift for growth and prosperity.'], 'Mrigashira' => ['Soma', 'a deer\'s head', 'Mrigashira is curious, gentle and always searching. Natives love travel, learning and exploring, and are sociable yet restless.'], 'Ardra' => ['Rudra', 'a teardrop', 'Ardra brings intensity, intelligence and transformation through storms. Natives are sharp thinkers who grow stronger after difficulties.'], 'Punarvasu' => ['Aditi', 'a bow and quiver', 'Punarvasu is the star of renewal and return. Natives are kind, optimistic and philosophical, and bounce back from any setback.'], 'Pushya' => ['Brihaspati', 'a cow\'s udder', 'Pushya is the most nourishing and auspicious nakshatra. Natives are caring, disciplined and religious, and are trusted by others.'], 'Ashlesha' => ['the Nagas', 'a coiled serpent', 'Ashlesha gives deep insight, cleverness and a hypnotic influence. Natives are perceptive and strategic but must guard against suspicion.'], 'Magha' => ['the Pitris (ancestors)', 'a throne', 'Magha is royal and linked with the ancestors. Natives are proud, dignified, respectful of tradition and born to lead.'], 'Purva Phalguni' => ['Bhaga', 'the front legs of a bed', 'Purva Phalguni loves pleasure, rest, art and romance. Natives are charming, generous and creative.'], 'Uttara Phalguni' => ['Aryaman', 'the back legs of a bed', 'Uttara Phalguni is the star of patronage and promises. Natives are helpful, reliable and kind, and do well in partnerships.'], 'Hasta' => ['Savitar', 'a hand', 'Hasta gives skill with the hands, wit and resourcefulness. Natives are clever and hard-working, and are good at crafts and healing.'], 'Chitra' => ['Vishwakarma', 'a bright jewel', 'Chitra is the star of the divine architect. Natives are creative and stylish, and are talented in design and building.'], 'Swati' => ['Vayu', 'a young shoot in the wind', 'Swati is independent, flexible and business-minded. Natives are diplomatic, love freedom and succeed through trade and balance.'], 'Vishakha' => ['Indra and Agni', 'a triumphal arch', 'Vishakha is goal-oriented and determined. Natives are ambitious and focused, and reach success after sustained effort.'], 'Anuradha' => ['Mitra', 'a lotus', 'Anuradha is the star of friendship and devotion. Natives are loyal and organised, and succeed through cooperation, often away from home.'], 'Jyeshtha' => ['Indra', 'an earring or umbrella', 'Jyeshtha is the star of seniority and protection. Natives are responsible and capable leaders, though they can feel burdened or become secretive.'], 'Mula' => ['Nirriti', 'a bunch of roots', 'Mula goes to the root of things. Natives are investigative and philosophical, and can rebuild life from its foundation.'], 'Purva Ashadha' => ['Apas (the waters)', 'a fan', 'Purva Ashadha is invincible and purifying. Natives are confident and persuasive, and proud of their beliefs.'], 'Uttara Ashadha' => ['the Vishwadevas', 'an elephant\'s tusk', 'Uttara Ashadha brings lasting victory. Natives are principled and responsible, and achieve steady, permanent success.'], 'Shravana' => ['Lord Vishnu', 'an ear', 'Shravana is the star of listening and learning. Natives are wise, well-informed and respectful of tradition, and make good teachers.'], 'Dhanishta' => ['the Ashta Vasus', 'a drum', 'Dhanishta brings wealth, rhythm and fame. Natives are musical, generous and energetic, and do well in groups.'], 'Shatabhisha' => ['Varuna', 'an empty circle', 'Shatabhisha is the star of a hundred healers. Natives are independent, private and scientific, and are gifted in healing or research.'], 'Purva Bhadrapada' => ['Aja Ekapada', 'a sword', 'Purva Bhadrapada is intense and idealistic. Natives are passionate and spiritual, and willing to sacrifice for a cause.'], 'Uttara Bhadrapada' => ['Ahir Budhnya', 'twins', 'Uttara Bhadrapada is calm, deep and wise. Natives are patient, disciplined and kind, and are spiritually inclined.'], 'Revati' => ['Pushan', 'a fish', 'Revati is the star of safe journeys and nourishment. Natives are gentle, generous, protective and artistic.']],
'dosha' => ['mangal' => 'Mangal Dosha is formed when Mars occupies certain houses from the ascendant or the Moon. Mars is a fiery planet, and in these houses it can bring haste, arguments and friction into married life. The dosha is often reduced by Mars\' sign, by a partner with a similar placement, and after the age of about twenty-eight. Patience in relationships and the remedies below are the practical answer.', 'kaal_sarp' => 'Kaal Sarp Dosha is formed when all seven planets fall on one side of the Rahu-Ketu axis. It can bring phases of sudden struggle and delay, followed by strong rises. Many successful people have this yoga; its effect depends on the houses involved and on the strength of the other planets.', 'sade_sati' => 'Sade Sati is the seven-and-a-half-year transit of Saturn over the twelfth, first and second signs from your Moon. It is a period of responsibility, lessons and hard work, and it often ends with lasting maturity and achievement. Honesty, discipline and Saturn remedies make it much lighter.', 'dhaiya' => 'Shani Dhaiya is the two-and-a-half-year transit of Saturn through the fourth or eighth sign from your Moon. It can bring pressure at home, on health or in work, and it asks for patience and careful decisions.', 'grahan' => 'Grahan Dosha is formed when the Sun or Moon is joined by Rahu or Ketu. It can cloud confidence (Sun) or peace of mind (Moon) and create confusion in the matters of that house. Regular worship, charity and a calm routine reduce its effect.', 'guru_chandal' => 'Guru Chandal Dosha is formed when Jupiter is joined by Rahu or Ketu. It can disturb judgement, faith and guidance from teachers. Respect for elders, clean habits and Jupiter remedies bring it back into balance.', 'kemadruma' => 'Kemadruma Dosha is formed when the Moon has no planet on either side of it. It can bring phases of loneliness or financial ups and downs. Strong planets elsewhere often cancel it, and Moon remedies help.', 'pitra' => 'Pitra Dosha points to unresolved karma of the ancestors. It can show as delays, obstacles in family progress or lack of results despite effort. Shraddha, feeding the needy and respect to elders are the traditional remedies.'],
'dignity' => ['exalted' => '{planet} is exalted here, at its strongest, and gives its best results with ease.', 'own' => '{planet} is in its own sign, comfortable and strong, and protects the matters of its house.', 'debilitated' => '{planet} is debilitated here, at its weakest, so its matters need extra effort and the remedies given below.', '' => '{planet} is in a neutral sign, so its results depend mainly on its house, its lordship and the running dasha.'],
't' => ['cover_title' => 'Janam Kundali and Life Report', 'cover_sub' => 'Vedic astrology · Lal Kitab · Remedies', 'prepared_for' => 'Prepared for', 'generated' => 'Generated on', 'contents' => 'Contents', 'ch_intro' => 'About this report', 'ch_birth' => 'Birth details and birth panchang', 'ch_charts' => 'Birth charts', 'ch_vargas' => 'Divisional charts (Vargas)', 'ch_lagna' => 'Your ascendant (Lagna)', 'ch_moon' => 'Your Moon sign (Rashi)', 'ch_nak' => 'Your birth star (Janma Nakshatra)', 'ch_planets' => 'The nine planets in your chart', 'ch_houses' => 'The twelve houses', 'ch_life' => 'Life areas', 'ch_yoga' => 'Yogas: special combinations', 'ch_dosha' => 'Doshas and karmic debts', 'ch_dasha' => 'Vimshottari Dasha: your planetary periods', 'ch_current' => 'Your current period', 'ch_transit' => 'Current transits (Gochar)', 'ch_varsh' => 'Varshphal: this year', 'ch_months' => 'Month-by-month guide', 'ch_remedy' => 'Remedies and upay', 'ch_lucky' => 'Lucky factors', 'ch_gloss' => 'Glossary', 'ch_note' => 'Important note', 'intro1' => 'This report is prepared from your date, time and place of birth. Your birth chart (Janam Kundali) is calculated with the sidereal zodiac and the Lahiri ayanamsa, the standard used across India, and the positions of the Sun, Moon, planets and the nodes Rahu and Ketu are worked out precisely for the moment you were born.', 'intro2' => 'The chart is then read using classical Vedic (Parashari) principles and the practical rules of Lal Kitab. Each planet is judged by its sign, house, dignity, nakshatra and the houses it rules. The Vimshottari dasha system is used for timing, and current transits and the yearly chart (Varshphal) show what is active now.', 'intro3' => 'Astrology shows tendencies, not fixed fate. Your own effort, choices and good deeds shape how these tendencies unfold. Read the strengths in this report as opportunities to use, and the challenges as areas to handle with care and simple remedies.', 'intro4' => 'How to read this report: begin with your ascendant, Moon sign and birth star, which describe your nature. Then read the planets and houses for the details of each area of life. The dasha chapters tell you when things are likely to happen, and the remedies chapter gives practical steps you can start today.', 'birth_intro' => 'The panchang at the moment of your birth describes the quality of that day. The weekday (vara), lunar day (tithi), birth star (nakshatra), yoga and karana together show the mood of time you were born into and are used in naming, muhurat and matching.', 'charts_intro' => 'The Lagna chart (D1) is the main birth chart and shows the whole life. The Navamsa (D9) shows the inner strength of planets, marriage and the second half of life. The Chandra chart treats the Moon\'s sign as the first house and shows how life feels from the mind\'s point of view.', 'vargas_intro' => 'Divisional charts (vargas) divide each sign into smaller parts to examine one area of life in detail: D2 for wealth, D3 for siblings, D7 for children, D9 for marriage, D10 for career, D12 for parents and so on. A planet that is strong in both D1 and the relevant varga gives the most reliable results.', 'lagna_lord' => 'Your lagna lord {lord} is placed in the {h} house in {sign}. The lagna lord is the captain of the chart, so this links your personality, health and life direction with {topics}. {q}', 'moon_intro' => 'Your Moon sign (rashi) is {sign}, and the Moon sits in your {h} house. The rashi is used for daily and monthly horoscopes, for Sade Sati and for many important decisions.', 'nak_intro' => 'You were born in {nak} nakshatra, pada {pada}. Its ruling planet is {lord}, its deity is {deity} and its symbol is {symbol}.', 'nak_dasha' => 'Because {lord} rules your birth star, your life began in the mahadasha of {lord}. The sequence of all later periods follows from this, as shown in the dasha chapter.', 'nak_pada' => 'The pada (quarter) you were born in adds the colour of the {navamsa} navamsa, refining how the qualities of this star express themselves in you.', 'p_place' => 'In your chart {planet} occupies {sign} in the {h} house ({hname}), the house of {topics}. {sign_nature}', 'p_lords' => '{planet} rules your house {houses}, so it carries the matters of {topics} into the {h} house where it sits.', 'p_nak' => 'It is placed in {nak} nakshatra, pada {pada}, ruled by {lord}. {nak_text}', 'p_retro' => '{planet} is retrograde, which turns its energy inward: its results may come after delays or second attempts, but with deeper understanding.', 'p_combust' => '{planet} is combust, too close to the Sun, which weakens its independent results; its matters need conscious care.', 'p_score' => 'Overall strength of {planet} in your chart: {score}/100 ({label}).', 'p_lk' => 'Lal Kitab reading', 'p_rem' => 'Remedies for {planet}', 'p_facts' => 'Planet at a glance', 'f_day' => 'Day', 'f_color' => 'Colour', 'f_gem' => 'Gemstone', 'f_metal' => 'Metal', 'f_grain' => 'Grain to donate', 'f_deity' => 'Deity', 'f_mantra' => 'Mantra', 'f_number' => 'Number', 'h_sign' => 'In your chart the sign {sign} falls on this house, ruled by {lord}. {sign_nature}', 'h_lord' => 'The lord of this house, {lord}, sits in your {h2} house, the house of {topics2}. This links the matters of this house with {topics2}.', 'h_lord_good' => 'This is a supportive placement, so the matters of this house tend to progress well and receive help.', 'h_lord_hard' => 'Because the lord sits in a house of challenge, results come after effort and patience; the remedies for {lord} help.', 'h_lord_mid' => 'Results come through steady effort and good timing, especially during the dasha of {lord}.', 'h_occ' => 'Planets in this house: {list}. Their nature colours these matters directly.', 'h_empty' => 'No planet occupies this house, so its results depend mainly on its lord {lord}, on the aspects it receives and on the running dasha.', 'h_occ_one' => '{planet} here brings its own themes into this house: {sig}', 'life_house' => 'Astrologically this area is read from your {h} house and its lord {lord}, which sits in the {h2} house.', 'yoga_present' => 'This yoga is present in your chart.', 'yoga_absent' => 'Yogas checked but not formed', 'yoga_rule' => 'How it is formed', 'yoga_effect' => 'What it gives', 'yoga_use' => 'Yogas show potential. They give their fullest results during the dasha or antardasha of the planets that form them, and when those planets are supported by transits. Good conduct and the remedies of these planets help the yoga to deliver.', 'dosha_present' => 'Present in your chart', 'dosha_absent' => 'Not present', 'dosha_effects' => 'Possible effects', 'dosha_remedy' => 'Remedy', 'rin_intro' => 'Lal Kitab describes karmic debts (rin) carried from the family line. A debt is indicated by specific planets in specific houses, and is cleared by a collective family remedy.', 'd_period' => '{from} to {to} · {years} years · age {a1} to {a2}', 'd_place' => 'In your chart {lord} sits in {sign} in the {h} house and rules house {houses}, so this period brings the matters of {topics} to the front.', 'd_pos' => 'Likely to go well', 'd_neg' => 'Needs care', 'd_ad' => 'Sub-periods (antardasha)', 'd_now' => 'current', 'cur_intro' => 'You are now running the mahadasha of {md} (until {md_to}) and the antardasha of {ad} (until {ad_to}).', 'cur_ad' => 'The antardasha lord {ad} adds its own flavour to the main period.', 'tr_intro' => 'Transits (gochar) are the current positions of the planets, counted from your Moon sign. Slow planets such as Saturn, Jupiter, Rahu and Ketu set the background for months or years, while the Sun, Mercury, Venus and Mars change the mood from week to week.', 'tr_row' => '{planet} is now transiting {sign}, the {hm} house from your Moon and the {hl} house from your lagna.', 'varsh_intro' => 'Varshphal (the annual chart) is cast for the moment the Sun returns to its exact birth position each year. It shows the themes of the current year of your life, from one birthday to the next. The Muntha shows the area of life that is highlighted this year.', 'month_intro' => 'The following pages give a guide for each of the next twelve months, based on the transits of the planets over your chart and your running dasha. Use the favourable months to begin important work, and the careful months for planning, finishing and remedies.', 'm_score' => 'Overall score: {score}/100 · {label}', 'rem_intro' => 'Remedies (upay) are simple actions that reduce the difficult effects of planets and strengthen the helpful ones. Begin with the priority remedies, follow them with faith and regularity, and remember that good conduct is the foundation of every remedy.', 'rem_priority' => 'Priority remedies for you', 'rem_life' => 'Lifelong Lal Kitab remedies', 'rem_gems' => 'Gemstones', 'rem_mantra' => 'Mantras for the planets that need support', 'rem_gem_note' => 'Wear a gemstone only after trying it for a few days and preferably after consulting an astrologer. Choose a natural, untreated stone of good quality, set it in the right metal, and energise it with the planet\'s mantra on the right day.', 'lucky_intro' => 'These lucky factors are drawn from the planets that are most helpful in your chart. Use them for important beginnings: interviews, agreements, purchases and journeys.', 'gloss' => [['Lagna (Ascendant)', 'The sign rising on the eastern horizon at birth. It forms the first house and describes body, personality and life direction.'], ['Rashi (Moon sign)', 'The sign occupied by the Moon at birth. It describes the mind and emotions and is used for horoscopes.'], ['Nakshatra', 'One of the 27 lunar mansions of 13°20\' each. The Moon\'s nakshatra at birth is the birth star.'], ['Bhava (House)', 'One of the twelve divisions of the chart, each ruling specific areas of life.'], ['Dasha', 'A planetary period. The Vimshottari system divides a 120-year cycle among the nine planets.'], ['Antardasha', 'A sub-period within a mahadasha, ruled by another planet.'], ['Gochar (Transit)', 'The current movement of the planets over your birth chart.'], ['Yoga', 'A special combination of planets that produces specific results.'], ['Dosha', 'An affliction formed by difficult planetary combinations, usually reduced by remedies.'], ['Varga', 'A divisional chart that examines one area of life in detail, such as the Navamsa (D9).'], ['Exalted / Debilitated', 'The sign where a planet is strongest / weakest.'], ['Retrograde (Vakri)', 'A planet that appears to move backwards from Earth; its results come with delay or re-effort.'], ['Upay', 'A remedy: a simple action, donation, mantra or discipline to balance a planet.']], 'note' => 'This report is generated from classical rules of Vedic astrology and Lal Kitab applied to your birth data. It is meant for guidance and self-understanding. It is not a substitute for medical, legal or financial advice, and no outcome is guaranteed. Always use your own judgement, and for important decisions consult qualified professionals.', 'house_n' => ['1st', '2nd', '3rd', '4th', '5th', '6th', '7th', '8th', '9th', '10th', '11th', '12th'], 'table_planet' => 'Planet', 'table_sign' => 'Sign', 'table_house' => 'House', 'table_deg' => 'Degree', 'table_nak' => 'Nakshatra', 'table_status' => 'Status', 'years' => 'years', 'strong' => 'strong', 'average' => 'average', 'weak' => 'weak'],
];
